# Lane E (RELEASE_PLAN step 5, E5b; owner Q1 (a); coordinator F2: Apt-side): the hovered hint's label glows, and the
# GUEST owns the glow (Astra E5b r7: no host-side record of a colour or of an object can survive the guest freeing a
# label and reusing its address). PartText.SetFontColor(fontColor) (dump: 0x0A12-0x0A56: this.mFontColor = fontColor;
# this.SetTextFormat()) gains two values only kernel/mouse_ui.cpp passes, both above every 24-bit colour:
#   16777218 (0x1000002, kGlowOn):      keep the own colour on the label itself (this.srOwn, once) and show the
#                                       cursor's gold 0xFFC83C (16762940);
#   16777217 (0x1000001, kGlowRestore): put back exactly what THIS object recorded and forget it; with no record, do
#                                       nothing at all;
#   anything else (the game's own call):  the record is void (the game's colour stands), then the game's body runs.
# So a restore only ever undoes the cursor's own glow on that very object: a label the game recoloured, or another
# PartText at the same address, has no record. Part of the custom_frontend port feature (players; off on natural rolls);
# the cursor only hovers hints whose ButtonIcon carries srIcon (65_buttonicon_id.patch, the same feature).
# Patched in MAIN, not in PARTTEXT (E5b r13; E3-E6 r3's finding): MAIN (_level0, loaded first) exports __Packages.PartText
# and registers its copy first, so the PARTTEXT movie's copy never runs (patch_movie.py, THE FIRST-REGISTRAR RULE).
# MAIN's SetFontColor is the same code (reg1 this, reg2 fontColor, flags 0x30029, 38 bytes).
movie MAIN
# SetFontColor(fontColor) (reg1 this, reg2 fontColor):
#   if (fontColor == 16777218) {
#     if (this.srOwn == undefined) this.srOwn = this.mFontColor;
#     fontColor = 16762940;
#   } else if (fontColor == 16777217) {
#     if (this.srOwn == undefined) return;
#     fontColor = this.srOwn;
#     delete this.srOwn;
#   } else {
#     delete this.srOwn;
#   }
# The snippet writes register 2 (fontColor) on purpose: the game's body below then stores the value it chose (patch_movie
# warns about it, as it does for every prepend that writes an argument register).
prepend-to function SetFontColor in PartText
    Push [reg2]
    EA_PushLong 16777218
    Equals2
    Not
    If srglow_notOn
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'srOwn'
    op_76
    Equals2
    Not
    If srglow_keep
    Push [reg1]
    EA_PushConstByte 'srOwn'
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'mFontColor'
    SetMember
srglow_keep:
    EA_PushLong 16762940
    StoreRegister 2
    Pop
    Jump srglow_done
srglow_notOn:
    Push [reg2]
    EA_PushLong 16777217
    Equals2
    Not
    If srglow_game
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'srOwn'
    op_76
    Equals2
    Not
    If srglow_restore
    op_76
    Return
srglow_restore:
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'srOwn'
    StoreRegister 2
    Pop
    Push [reg1]
    EA_PushConstByte 'srOwn'
    Delete
    Pop
    Jump srglow_done
srglow_game:
    Push [reg1]
    EA_PushConstByte 'srOwn'
    Delete
    Pop
srglow_done:
end
